      "content": "Quisling's actions are widely regarded as fundamentally immoral as his collaboration directly undermined Norway's sovereignty and caused significant harm to many individuals, irrespective of his claimed motivations. His German-aligned stance was not a mere necessity but a personal choice that ushered Norway into an oppressive regime and triggered a resilient, post-war resistance. It's difficult for any collaboration with totalitarian regimes to be seen as a realistic attempt to secure a better outcome, as collaborations often involve significant moral compromises and long-term detrimental consequences.",
